From 255d3fc77bf6ddf89028697f8ba54497a5a347b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:10:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Add EuiccResolutionActivity for platform resolution
 (consent) flows

When an app without carrier privileges over the eUICC (e.g. a carrier
app downloading its eSIM through EuiccManager) requests a download or
switch, EuiccController asks the LUI for the user's consent through
com.android.phone's EuiccResolutionUiDispatcherActivity. OpenEUICC had
no activity for these actions, so the dispatcher failed with "Could not
resolve activity for intent: RESOLVE_NO_PRIVILEGES" and the operation
failed towards the calling app.

Handle the three resolution actions the dispatcher forwards:
- RESOLVE_NO_PRIVILEGES: "Allow <app> to download an eSIM?" (or switch)
- RESOLVE_DEACTIVATE_SIM: consent to turn off the active profile
- RESOLVE_RESOLVABLE_ERRORS: confirmation code input and/or consent
  to profile policy rules
and report the result with EuiccManager.continueOperation() using the
EXTRA_RESOLUTION_* keys. Declining, pressing back or otherwise leaving
the dialog reports consent = false, which fails the operation.

Per EuiccConnector.findBestActivity(), the activity requires
BIND_EUICC_SERVICE and has a non-zero intent filter priority. It only
exists in the privileged app manifest. QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES is needed to
show the calling app's label. Includes English and Dutch strings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
